Below is a **stand‑alone validation script** you can drop into the project root (e.g., `test-env-connectivity.js`).  
Running it will attempt a minimal operation against each of the external services listed in `.env.test` and will log a green “✅” if the call succeeded, or a red “❌” with the error message if it failed.

> **⚠️ Note** – The credentials in `.env.test` are deliberately “canary” values so you’ll almost certainly see failures unless you replace them with real keys.  The purpose of the script is to illustrate how you would automatically verify that each key is still functional before deploying.

